A||N||7||foxgapfiero||Power lock fix||||1||
Z||000000||foxgapfiero||09-27-2001||06:15 PM||||This weekend I'm going to try to adjust and lube the power locks on my 86 GT. The question is what do I adjust and what do I lube? The darn things take about 4 pushes of the button to release the lock. Any help will be much apprieciated.   Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mark||09-27-2001||07:11 PM||||Take the inner door panel off.  Operate the power lock and notice what moves (or tries to move).  Spray those parts with something like WD40.  Also spray the key cylinder while you're at it.  Power lock should work much better.||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||09-27-2001||07:33 PM||||yep I dont think that there is any thing to adjust.just lube ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GarethWright||09-28-2001||01:49 AM||||It also could be a load of "crap" in the switch itself, too much dust and crud between the contacts and it won't throw the switch. (until you grind it out of the way a bit) but when yur done, be sure to use some of that electric grease stuff and lube it back up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierogtracer||09-28-2001||03:59 AM||||Just a couple of tips on items to use. Quick dry electrical connector cleaner and white grease spray. Spray all the "gunked" parts with the cleaner will not hurt anything in the system. White grease just plain last longer than most WD40 type lubricants.<P>My 2cents<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_11.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FullRaceCam||09-29-2001||08:45 PM||||WD40 is actually a solvent and not a lubricant and shouldn't be used for as an alternative to the proper kind of grease. WD40 will not last any resonablelength of time. That's why it will clean your hands up so nice after a day in the shop.||||reg||1
Z||000006||MontanaFiero||09-30-2001||01:46 AM||||Also, don't use WD-40 on the lock cylinders. Use graphite.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||foxgapfiero||09-30-2001||08:06 AM||||Just wanted to let everyone know the repair of the door locks has been 75% effective. the 25% that did not work eas that the pass. door selinoid is getting weak. After lubing and cleaning the lock still would not operate as well as the drivers door. So as a quick fix until I get a new selinoid I bent the small rocker arm that makes the door lock and unlock a tiny bit and now the door unlocks fine but you still have to hit the button twice to lock it.<P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
